{
  "name": "rust-signals",
  "description": "rust-signals (distributed as futures-signals) is a zero-cost Functional Reactive Programming (FRP) library for Rust that implements efficient state propagation through a poll-based model integrated with the futures ecosystem. It provides specialized traits and data structures—Signal, SignalVec, and SignalMap—to track and communicate changes in scalars and collections with minimal runtime overhead. The architecture leverages the standard Waker mechanism to ensure that consumers only react when values have changed, maintaining strong performance characteristics for GUI synchronization and real-time state management.",
